---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StaticPage from '../components/StaticPage.astro';

const updated = '15 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — DivyaKatha"
  description="How DivyaKatha collects and uses information, including Google Analytics."
>
  <StaticPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="A plain-language summary of what we collect on this site and why."
  >
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      DivyaKatha (<a href="/">divyakatha</a>) is a personal blog about temple tales and Hindu folklore,
      run by <strong>Rishabh Anand</strong>. This page explains what information may be collected when
      you visit the site and how it is used.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you browse DivyaKatha, the following may be collected automatically:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage data</strong> — pages viewed, approximate location (country/region), device and
        browser type, screen size, referral source, and time spent on pages.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics identifiers</strong> — Google Analytics may set cookies or similar technologies
        to distinguish visits and measure traffic. Our measurement ID is
        <strong>G-S7DXESED8M</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs</strong> — our hosting provider may record standard technical logs (such as
        IP address and request time) for security and reliability.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not run a user account system on this site. If you email us, we receive whatever you choose
      to send (your email address, name, and message content).
    </p>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To understand which stories readers find useful and how the site is used.</li>
      <li>To keep the site secure, stable, and fast.</li>
      <li>To respond if you contact us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may introduce advertising (for example, Google AdSense) in the future if readership grows.
      If that happens, this policy will be updated to describe any additional data collection.
      Advertising is <strong>not</strong> active on the site today.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://analytics.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Analytics</a>
      (Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC) to measure site traffic. Google processes usage data on our
      behalf as a service provider. You can read how Google handles data in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Analytics data is typically retained according to Google's settings for this property; we
      review aggregated reports rather than trying to identify individual visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Content from our CMS</h2>
    <p>
      Blog posts and images may be served from our content backend (Strapi at
      <code>cms.sibani-panigrahy.com</code>). Visiting a page that loads those assets may result in
      standard web requests to that host.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal basis (for visitors in the EU/UK)</h2>
    <p>
      We rely on <strong>legitimate interests</strong> to operate and improve a small editorial website,
      and on <strong>consent</strong> where required for non-essential cookies. You can limit analytics
      cookies via your browser settings (see our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask what personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Request correction or deletion of information we control.</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict certain processing.</li>
      <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise these rights, email
      <a href="mailto:admin@rishabh-anand.com">admin@rishabh-anand.com</a>. We will respond within a
      reasonable time. We may need to verify your request.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      DivyaKatha is intended for a general audience. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from children under 13. If you believe a child has contacted us with personal data, please email us
      and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when the site changes. The "last updated" date at the top will reflect
      the latest version. Continued use of the site after changes means you accept the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Rishabh Anand</strong><br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:admin@rishabh-anand.com">admin@rishabh-anand.com</a><br />
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>
    </p>
  </StaticPage>
</Base>
